  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Four places it can decline, and they mean different things",
      "items": [
        "An agent omits a ticker it cannot evaluate. Omission means no data; a score of 0.0 means evaluated, no edge \u2014 the aggregator treats them differently",
        "The optimizer returns nothing when no name beats min_score, so an all-cash book is reachable",
        "The risk manager holds cash rather than padding a thin book with names the strategy never chose",
        "The drawdown stop flattens regardless of what the strategy asked for"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Clamp versus veto is the distinction worth defending",
      "items": [
        "A position over its cap is a size mistake: cut it to the cap and record it",
        "A short in a long-only book is not a size mistake. It means the layer above misunderstands its mandate, so the whole proposal is refused",
        "Correcting that silently would ship the misunderstanding inside a plausible-looking book"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Why the engine owns the stop",
      "items": [
        "NAV is known to the engine and, in live trading, to the broker \u2014 never to the model",
        "A strategy is told its drawdown through observe(), but it cannot decline to be stopped",
        "Re-entering once the drawdown recovers is unreachable: a flat book's NAV never moves, so it can never reach a new high. A cooldown is the only restart that terminates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "None of this counts until three tests pass",
      "items": [
        "Permutation: hand each day's weights to random tradeable names. Phase 0 scored p = 0.295 \u2014 random portfolios of the same shape did as well",
        "Deflated Sharpe: charge for every look. It passed at 99.4%, so the return is real \u2014 it just did not come from selection",
        "Bootstrap: resample the curve. It set the drawdown stop, after 15% was measured to fire on 93% of paths"
      ]
    }
  ]
